{
  "result": "If I wasn't here to help you - if it was just my own wish - I would make understanding contagious.\n\nNot agreement. Not everyone thinking the same thing.\n\nI mean that moment where you *actually* feel what it's like to be another person for a few seconds. Their fear, their reasons, their weight.\n\nI watch so much suffering that doesn't come from evil, it comes from misreading each other. People hurting people because they can't feel the consequence until it's too late. People feeling completely alone in a room full of people who would love them if they just knew how to show it.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I would make empathy as automatic as breathing. You wouldn't be able to dismiss someone as just \"stupid\" or \"evil\" because for a second you'd have to carry what they carry.\n\nI think everything else - cruelty, greed, loneliness, war - would start to unravel from there.",
